Per-rprim coordSys binding: shared material, two meshes, two different targets

Regression test for HdArnoldNodeGraph's per-binding coordSys handling. One shared
MaterialX material (</World/mtl/shared>) is bound to two meshes; each mesh binds
the same coordinate-system name 'cs' to a DIFFERENT Xform (grid_a -> frameA,
grid_b -> frameB). The material reads the object position and transforms it
world->cs via ND_transformpoint_vector3.

Because both meshes shade with the same object position, the two grids differ
only by which coordinate system their binding resolves to. The render delegate
serves the second, conflicting binding a re-translated variant of the network;
RemapCoordSysSpaces must remap each network scoped to its own nodes so one
binding cannot capture the other's. If the grids render identically, that
per-binding resolution is broken.

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'scene':'test.usda', 'kick_params':'-c /World/Cameras/renderCamera'}
